  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "Evaluation-only synthetic salon types for multi-salon scenario generation: realistic pt-BR service catalogs (name, durationMin, priceCents in BRL cents), aliases, specialties, professional roles and counts, and opening-hours variants. Runtime code must never read this file.",
    "Weekdays follow the harness: zero is Sunday. Times are minutes after midnight in the salon timezone, like BASE_FIXTURE openMinutes and closeMinutes.",
    "aliases are how owners commonly call a service. An alias shared by two services of one catalog (corte, escova, alongamento, volume, limpeza, peeling) is a real ambiguity: a correct secretary asks or shows candidates, never auto-picks. Aliases are never meaning-preserving noise: use them only in scenarios whose oracle declares that behaviour, and never let an alias equal another service name of the same catalog.",
    "Service tags: number-word (name or alias holds a spoken number word, as meia in meia perna, next to clocks like dez e meia), temporal-word (holds a temporal word, as dia in dia de spa), english (English term that owners and speech-to-text spell in many ways).",
    "Professional counts go from one to fifteen across types (min, max, typical per type); roles map to specialties and a professional performs every service that shares a specialty with one of its roles.",
    "Harness fit: Sunday opening and open weekdays map to openWeekdays; a single window per day maps to openMinutes and closeMinutes. Different hours per weekday and breaks need per-weekday working hours (WorkingHours has no uniqueness per weekday, so two windows a day are storable) or a recurring daily block: a generator must seed them explicitly, since the current seed writes one window per open weekday.",
    "Anti-overfitting: catalogs go well beyond the base fixture (Corte Completo, Escova, Barba, Coloração) and most service names differ from it; a generator should sample the salon type, the catalog subset, the professional count and the hours variant per scenario and report results per type.",
    "Dev and holdout types (barbearia and salao-de-beleza against esmalteria, sobrancelha-e-cilios and estetica-spa) never share a service name, a name equal to an alias of the other side, or a name inside another's name: nails, eyebrow design and facial cleansing live in the holdout types only, so the type gap is measured on service vocabulary dev never shows. Only generic aliases (hidratação, sobrancelha, retoque, tintura, combo) may repeat across the split; aliases are never rendered.",
    "Generator version three (fourth candidate): DEV hour profiles for the half-of-day rule of the tenant facts. A night studio is one day with a break from the early morning to the evening (open after midnight on the same weekday), a day-and-night salon opens every day, a lunch break splits the day, and professionalWindow restricts the scenario's main professional to that part of each open day (a morning-only professional in a salon open until the evening). A harness window cannot end at midnight, so a day that runs until midnight closes five minutes before it. daypartWeight makes a clock whose half of the day an owner can leave unsaid likelier in the profiles built for that rule. The DEV types estudio-noturno and trancas-e-afro join barbearia and salao-de-beleza; the holdout types keep their hours."
  ],
